 ## Decision tables
 
-### Classify an artifact
+### Tool verdict (`tools/souji-verify.sh`)
 
 | Observation | Verdict |
 |---|---|
-| Owning repo has unpushed commits touching the artifact's path, or a dirty worktree over it | `NOT-SAFE` — live work; record and skip |
-| Artifact's last commit is an ancestor of `origin/<default>` | `SAFE(pushed)` — removable after quarantine |
-| Ledger row matches path + hash | `SAFE(moved-to-obsidian)` — source copy removable |
-| Scratch type + zero live references + older than lane's last admitted round | `SAFE(stale)` — removable |
-| Anything else, any doubt, any credential-shaped content | `NOT-SAFE` — stay silent in the dry run |
+| Path component matches `*.env`, `.env`, `.env.*`, `.envrc`, `*credential*`, `*secret*`, `id_*`, `*.pem` (even if the path is missing) | `NOT-SAFE(secrets-refusal)` — do not read it |
+| Path missing | `NOT-SAFE(unreachable)` |
+| Directory containing `.git` (repo root) | ledger only, else `NOT-SAFE` with `unpushed=N dirty=M`. The tool does not emit `SAFE(pushed)` for a repo root. Trust a ledger SAFE only after vault-verify agrees |
+| Worktree registration, named branch, unpushed commits > 0 | `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)` — checked before the absent-directory shortcut |
+| Worktree registration, directory absent, unique commits = 0, named-branch check clear | `SAFE(metadata-prune)` |
+| Worktree registration, directory present and dirty | `NOT-SAFE(dirty)` |
+| Worktree registration, directory present and clean | `NOT-SAFE(none)` — not removable (`evaluate_worktree` in `tools/souji-verify.sh`) |
+| Introducing commit is an ancestor of the resolved `refs/remotes/origin/*` ref, path exists | `SAFE(pushed)`. This does not check a dirty worktree |
+| No remote-tracking ref, introducing commit exists | `NOT-SAFE(pushed-unverifiable)` |
+| Ledger row matches both hashes | tool may print `SAFE(moved-to-obsidian)`. Trust it only if `souji-vault-verify.sh` prints `VERIFIED(moved-to-obsidian)` |
+| Scratch family, tool ref count 0, older than `--stale-days` | tool may print `SAFE(stale)`. Trust it only after the operator `--hidden` sweep |
+| Anything else | `NOT-SAFE` |
